---
import PolicyPageLayout from '../components/PolicyPageLayout.astro';

const toc = [
  { id: 'definitions', label: 'What are cookies and browser storage?' },
  { id: 'technologies', label: 'Technologies used' },
  { id: 'calculator-storage', label: 'Calculator sessionStorage' },
  { id: 'turnstile-storage', label: 'Turnstile' },
  { id: 'analytics-marketing', label: 'Analytics and marketing' },
  { id: 'managing-storage', label: 'Managing browser storage' },
  { id: 'changes', label: 'Changes to this policy' },
] as const;
---

<PolicyPageLayout
  title="Cookie and Browser Storage Policy | All Yacht Service"
  description="Learn which cookies and browser-storage technologies are used by the All Yacht Service website and how they support essential functions."
  heading="Cookie and Browser Storage Policy"
  intro="This policy describes the limited browser-storage and security technologies currently used by the All Yacht Service website."
  pathname="/cookie-policy"
  routeId="cookiePolicy"
  toc={toc}
>
  <section id="definitions" aria-labelledby="definitions-heading">
    <h2 id="definitions-heading">1. What Are Cookies and Browser Storage?</h2>
    <p>
      Cookies are small values that a website or service may ask a browser to
      store and send with later requests. <code>sessionStorage</code> is a separate
      browser feature that stores data for one tab’s browsing session and does not
      automatically accompany network requests. Security services may also use short-lived
      browser tokens and technical signals without those values being marketing cookies.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="technologies" aria-labelledby="technologies-heading">
    <h2 id="technologies-heading">2. Technologies Used</h2>
    <p>
      The following inventory is based on the current source code. It should be
      re-audited before adding scripts, embeds, analytics, advertising or
      consent tooling.
    </p>
    <div
      class="policy-table-scroll"
      role="region"
      aria-label="Cookie and browser storage inventory"
      tabindex="0"
    >
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Name or technology</th>
            <th scope="col">Provider</th>
            <th scope="col">Purpose</th>
            <th scope="col">Type</th>
            <th scope="col">Duration</th>
            <th scope="col">Consent required</th>
            <th scope="col">Where used</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row"><code>ays:pre-purchase-survey-estimate:v1</code></th
            >
            <td>All Yacht Service</td>
            <td>Transfers a survey estimate to the Contact form.</td>
            <td>Essential <code>sessionStorage</code></td>
            <td>Browser session; accepted by the application for 24 hours.</td>
            <td>No</td>
            <td>Survey calculator and Contact form</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row"><code>ays:yacht-delivery-estimate:v1</code></th>
            <td>All Yacht Service</td>
            <td>Transfers a yacht-delivery estimate to the Contact form.</td>
            <td>Essential <code>sessionStorage</code></td>
            <td>Browser session; accepted by the application for 24 hours.</td>
            <td>No</td>
            <td>Delivery calculator and Contact form</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row"
              >Turnstile verification token and technical signals</th
            >
            <td>Cloudflare</td>
            <td>Protects the Contact form from automated abuse.</td>
            <td>Strictly necessary security service</td>
            <td
              >Short-lived token; any additional storage depends on the
              configured Cloudflare widget and browser context.</td
            >
            <td>No, for the current security purpose</td>
            <td>Contact form</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="calculator-storage" aria-labelledby="calculator-storage-heading">
    <h2 id="calculator-storage-heading">3. Calculator sessionStorage</h2>
    <p>
      The two calculator keys temporarily hold the selected route, vessel,
      options, estimate, creation time and reference needed to show a result in
      the Contact form. They do not contain Contact-form personal details such
      as your name, email, phone or message.
    </p>
    <p>
      The application rejects records older than 24 hours, even if a browser
      happens to retain them. The browser normally removes session storage when
      the relevant tab or session ends. You can remove a transferred estimate in
      the Contact form without sending it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="turnstile-storage" aria-labelledby="turnstile-storage-heading">
    <h2 id="turnstile-storage-heading">4. Turnstile</h2>
    <p>
      Cloudflare Turnstile runs browser checks and creates a token that the
      server validates before accepting a Contact submission. The repository
      uses implicit rendering with the <code>contact</code> action and light theme.
      It does not explicitly select invisible or non-interactive mode, and it does
      not configure pre-clearance in source code.
    </p>
    <p>
      Widget type and account-level pre-clearance settings are controlled in
      Cloudflare and must be confirmed there before production. This inventory
      therefore does not list <code>cf_clearance</code> as definitely used and does
      not invent provider cookie names. See Cloudflare’s
      <a
        href="https://www.cloudflare.com/turnstile-privacy-policy/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">Turnstile Privacy Addendum (external link)</a
      >.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section
    id="analytics-marketing"
    aria-labelledby="analytics-marketing-heading"
  >
    <h2 id="analytics-marketing-heading">5. Analytics and Marketing</h2>
    <p>
      The website does not currently use analytics or advertising cookies. The
      current source also contains no marketing tags or social-media embeds.
      Images are served locally, and fonts use the visitor’s installed system
      fonts.
    </p>
    <p>
      If analytics or marketing technologies are introduced, this policy and any
      required consent controls must be updated before activation.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="managing-storage" aria-labelledby="managing-storage-heading">
    <h2 id="managing-storage-heading">6. Managing Browser Storage</h2>
    <p>
      Browser settings generally allow you to inspect or clear cookies and site
      data. Closing the relevant tab or browser session normally clears
      <code>sessionStorage</code>. Blocking strictly necessary storage or
      security features may prevent calculator transfer or Contact-form
      submission. Consult the current help documentation for your browser or
      device for exact controls.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="changes" aria-labelledby="cookie-changes-heading">
    <h2 id="cookie-changes-heading">7. Changes</h2>
    <p>
      This policy and its review date will be updated before a new storage,
      analytics, advertising, embed or consent technology is activated, and
      whenever the current technical inventory changes materially.
    </p>
  </section>
</PolicyPageLayout>
